message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite a fixed release of This Is Not The Xealeus Engine."
title: "This Is Not The Xealeus Engine"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Xealeus"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-11-02
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23903877"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/xealeus/This-Is-Not-The-Xealeus-Engine"
url: "https://github.com/xealeus/This-Is-Not-The-Xealeus-Engine"
abstract: >-
  A guided graphical companion to the Xealeus Voynich computational experiments,
  demonstrating parser checks, Prefix/Core/Suffix coupling, Currier A/B transfer,
  local state-machine compilers, cross-word dependencies, and a simple 2D geometry
  probe using bundled project-derived aggregate data or an independently supplied
  compatible IVTFF source corpus.
keywords:
  - "Voynich Manuscript"
  - "computational analysis"
  - "statistical modelling"
  - "state machine"
  - "EVA"
  - "Currier A"
  - "Currier B"
  - "reproducible research"
